# XCU sh-patterns
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XCU.sh-patterns.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.14.1
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.14.2
class      required
says       Ordinary characters match themselves, ? matches exactly one
           character, * matches any string including the empty one (each *
           as much as lets the rest match).
test       t/001-ordinary-star-question.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-patterns.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.14.1
class      required
says       Bracket expressions match one character from a list, a range or a
           class, ! negates, a ] first and a - first or last are literal.
test       t/002-brackets.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-patterns.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.14.1/does not introduce a valid bracket expression
class      required
says       A [ that does not start a valid bracket expression matches a [
           itself.
test       t/003-bracket-not-valid.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-patterns.004
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.14.1
class      required
says       A quoted or backslash-escaped pattern character matches only
           itself; a pattern that comes from an expansion keeps its special
           characters unless the expansion was quoted.
test       t/004-quoting.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-patterns.005
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.14.1
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.14.3
class      required
says       Matching is by characters and is case-sensitive; in a case
           pattern (not filename expansion) * and ? and [/] also match a
           slash or a leading period.
test       t/005-case-sensitive-slash-period.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-patterns.006
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.14.3/sorted according to the collating sequence
class      required
says       Pathname expansion replaces a pattern that matches existing names
           by those names, sorted by the collating sequence (byte order in
           the POSIX locale).
test       t/006-expand-sorted.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-patterns.007
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.14.3/If the pattern does not match any
class      required
says       A pattern that matches no name is left as it is; a word with no
           pattern characters is also left alone.
test       t/007-expand-no-match.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-patterns.008
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.14.3/slash
class      required
says       In pathname expansion a slash is matched only by a slash in the
           pattern, never by *, ? or a bracket expression, and a [ with a
           slash before its ] is an ordinary character.
test       t/008-expand-slash.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-patterns.009
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.14.3/leading
class      required
says       A leading period in a name is matched only by an explicit period
           in the pattern (first, or just after a slash), not by *, ?, [!a],
           or a range.
test       t/009-expand-leading-period.sh

assertion  XCU.sh-patterns.010
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.14.1
class      required
says       Quoted or escaped pattern characters are not expanded as filename
           patterns.
test       t/010-expand-quoted-literal.sh
